  "name": "The Deep Sea and Its Ground and Temperature Conditions",
  "description": "Publication Title: \"Sammlung Gemein Verstandlicher Wisseuschaftlicher Vortrage\" (Collection of Scientific Lectures). Volume XIII No. 289-312, pages 821-884. Lecture title: \"Die Tiefsee und Ihre Boden- und Temperatur- Verhaltnisse\" (\"The Deep-Sea and Its Ground and Temperature Conditions\"). Author: Boguslawski, G. Von. Text in German. Information in this collection dates back to the 18th century for daily, monthly, seasonal, and annual tabular summaries, and the 19th century for weather maps. In these summaries, definitions are: 1. Hourly/daily/monthly/seasonal/annual data -- values determined for each consecutive period, e.g. monthly temperature data: Jan 1900, Feb 1900, etc. 2. Long-term data -- values determined over a period of years, e.g. long-term monthly temperature data using Jan 1901, Jan 1902, etc. This book contains tables of hourly sea surface and subsurface temperature recorded at 3 ships during voyages round the world in Pacific, Atlantic, and Indian Oceans, from 1873 through 1876. Also contains conditions of the sea floor ocean circulation and temperature distribution. Graphs contain the following data: - hourly sea surface and subsurface temperature Maps contain the following data: - depths of Pacific, Atlantic, and Indian Oceans.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: This book is a part of the foreign meteorological data collection held by the NOAA Central Library in Washington, DC.",
